{"content":{"result":[{"rank_order":1,"title":"AWS Elemental MediaTailor Monetization Functions adds ad response hooks - AWS","context":"AWS Elemental MediaTailor, a video service offered by Amazon Web Services (AWS), has introduced two new monetization functions: post ad decision server (ADS) response and pre manifest insertion. MediaTailor personalizes and inserts ads into live and on-demand streams, and these functions allow customers to run custom logic at defined points in an ad-personalized playback session. The post ADS response hook runs after MediaTailor parses an ADS response and resolves all VAST wrappers, enabling customers to call a secondary ad source when the primary one returns insufficient demand, remove disallowed ads based on content or brand policies, and add house ads or promotions from their marketing systems. The pre manifest insertion hook runs at the last point before MediaTailor returns the ad pod to the viewer, allowing customers to make a final check on what is about to play and insert personalized slates when necessary. Both hooks are fail-open, meaning they discard the function output and continue with default ad insertion on a timeout, expression error, or resource limit. These hooks are available in all AWS Regions where MediaTailor is available. To learn more, customers can refer to the Monetization Functions section in the AWS Elemental MediaTailor User Guide and the MediaTailor pricing page. To get started, they should sign in to the AWS Elemental MediaTailor console. MediaTailor is available in all AWS Regions where it is offered. For a complete list, customers can check the AWS Regional Services List","url":"https://aws.amazon.com/about-aws/whats-new/2026/09/aws-elemental-mediatailor-functions-ad-response-hooks/"},{"rank_order":2,"title":"AWS Elemental MediaTailor now supports Low-Latency HLS ad insertion - AWS","context":"AWS Elemental MediaTailor now supports low-latency HTTP Live Streaming (LL-HLS) ad insertion using HLS Interstitials. MediaTailor is a service for video providers to monetize live streams, linear channels, and video-on-demand content. LL-HLS reduces live latency by delivering partial segments and keeping media playlists cacheable at CDN edges. MediaTailor uses HLS Interstitials to reference ads as separate playlists, allowing for low-latency playback at scale and moving ad decision server calls off the manifest request path. This capability is ideal for live sports, news, betting and wagering, watch-party, and interactive live formats. Low-latency HLS ad insertion is available in all AWS Regions where MediaTailor is available. For more information, visit the MediaTailor product page and server-guided ad insertion documentation. To get started, sign in to the MediaTailor console. MediaTailor supports LL-HLS by delivering partial segments and keeping media playlists cacheable at CDN edges, using HLS Interstitials to reference ads as separate playlists, and moving ad decision server calls off the manifest request path. This results in low-latency playback at scale, making it suitable for live events and interactive formats where latency is crucial. The feature is currently available in all AWS Regions where MediaTailor is offered. For further details, interested parties can refer to the MediaTailor product page and server-guided ad insertion documentation and sign in to the MediaTailor console to get started","url":"https://aws.amazon.com/about-aws/whats-new/2026/09/aws-elemental-mediatailor-low-latency-hls-ad-insertion/"},{"rank_order":3,"title":"troubleshooting-efs","skill_description":"Diagnoses and resolves Amazon EFS issues including mount failures, NFS timeouts, permission errors, throughput problems, and burst credit exhaustion. Use when the user has an EFS file system that is not mounting, returning errors, performing slowly, or showing access denied.\n\n\nServices: efs, ec2, iam, kms, vpc, cloudwatch\nTasks: debug, troubleshoot, diagnose\nPersona: developer, devops\nWorkload: storage\n*","skill_name":"troubleshooting-efs"},{"rank_order":4,"title":"troubleshooting-s3-files","skill_description":"Diagnoses and resolves Amazon S3 Files issues including mount failures, permission errors, synchronization problems, and performance issues. Use when the user has an S3 file system that is not mounting, returning access denied, not syncing changes to S3, showing files in lost+found, or performing slower than expected.\n\n\nServices: s3, s3files, efs, iam, kms, cloudwatch\nTasks: debug, troubleshoot, diagnose\nPersona: developer, devops\nWorkload: storage\n*","skill_name":"troubleshooting-s3-files"},{"rank_order":5,"title":"securing-s3-buckets","skill_description":"Create and secure S3 buckets following AWS best practices for access control, encryption, monitoring, and remediation of misconfigurations. Use when the user wants to secure a new bucket, audit an existing bucket, fix a security finding, configure encryption, or enable logging and monitoring. Do NOT use for general S3 data operations, S3 Tables setup, or discovering existing data assets.\n\n\nServices: s3, kms, cloudtrail, guardduty, config, accessanalyzer\nTasks: secure, audit, remediate, encrypt, monitor\nPersona: developer, security-engineer\nWorkload: storage, compliance\n*","skill_name":"securing-s3-buckets"}]}}"}]}], "label": "Look up AWS MediaTailor docs on session expiration causing HTTP 400 after pause."}
